<title>MALAYSIA: Shell in Malaysia to lay off 400.</title>
<headline>Shell in Malaysia to lay off 400.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-09-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 400 employees of Sarawak Shell Bhd in eastern Sarawak state will be retrenched from Monday, the national Bernama news agency said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The employees are from Shell's clerical and operations department category, mid-level supervisors and specialist staff as well as senior staff, it said quoting company employees.</p>
<p>Sarawak Shell and Sabah Shell Petroleum Co in July said it would lay off 600 employees by December this year.</p>
<p>This was part of a major reorganisation aimed at maintaining its profits and growth amid weak oil prices and tough compeitition, a company statement had said.</p>
<p>Sarawak Shell and Sabah Shell are the Malaysian exploration companies of the Royal Dutch Shell Group.</p>
</text>
